the bad batch is a love letter to star  wars continuity and the more you know  about the series the more you'll get out  of it  after all the show is packed with small  details designed to get hardcore fans  and a tizzy  here are a few examples you might have  missed the bad batch pilot pays tribute  to its clone wars legacy right off the  bat  first the clone wars logo appears on  screen only to be burned away and  replaced by the bad batch insignia the  first episode of the bad batch then  launches into a saturday morning serial  inspired recap just like the ones that  kick off every episode of the clone wars  as on the clone wars the opening  voiceover is performed by actor tom kane  who also played yoda on the older series  however in late 2020 kane tragically  suffered a stroke inhibiting his ability  to speak which may unfortunately soon  lead to his retirement from voice acting  if that's the case the bad batch opening  isn't just a nice way to bridge the gap  between the two shows  it's also a wonderful tribute to one of  the star wars animated series signature  voices solidifying kane's legacy in a  galaxy far far away  officially the bad batch isn't actually  called the bad batch  in the republic and later imperial  records the group of misfit clones is  actually known as clone force 99  as clone wars viewers know that's a  number loaded with significance  i am merely stating a scientific  hypothesis based on factual data  in the season 3 clone wars episode clone  cadets which is chronologically speaking  the first time that we meet bad batch  member echo were introduced to a clone  known as 99  compared to the other clones he's a  little different something went wrong  during 99's creation and he was plagued  by a number of genetic defects that  rendered him unfit for duty  he basically became a glorified janitor  in camino home of the republic's cloning  facilities  99's hearts however worked just fine  despite staying away from the front  lines 99 considered all clones  particularly those still in training as  his brothers and ultimately gave up his  life to keep them safe  clone cadets is actually the first time  in star wars canon that we hear someone  use the phrase bad batch which is said  in reference to ekko and his original  team  it makes sense that the republic squad  made up of divergent clones would name  themselves after the most beloved of  their number  however the name clone force 99 also has  more sinister connotations  if you turn 99 upside down you get 66  the name of the top secret order that  resulted in the jedi's extinction at the  clone's hands  the bad match is about everyday soldiers  in the trenches not the high and mighty  battles bought by the jedi in the sith  but you'll still see a few  lightsabers in the latest star wars  cartoon the series pilot for example  gives us an up close and personal look  at how clone force 99 reacted to  palpatine's order 66  by detailing the execution of jedi  master depa billaba and the escape of  her padawan caleb dune  of course if you're all caught up in the  animated star wars shows you know caleb  by a different name  kanan jarrus which is the identity he  uses in star wars rebels where he leads  the titular group of freedom fighters  interestingly this is actually the  second time we've seen kanan's brush  with order 66.  the 2015 marvel comic mini-series kane  in the last padawan shows us a slightly  different version of these events  in the comic blabba tells kanyon that  she'll be right behind him as he flees  and the bad batch itself isn't seen  still it seems like the bad batch  creative team had the comic in mind  while designing the scene  the clones hunting caleb in the last  padawan had red markings that recall the  paint on the bad batch's armor  while one of the republic soldiers  hunting caleb says good soldiers follow  orders  a line repeated by crosshair in the bad  match pilot  once a bad batch returned to camino but  before crosshair betrays them and  they're forced to go on the run the  defective clones spend a little bit of  time unwinding in their quarters  there's no doubt that the clones have  made the room their own on textbunk for  example you can see schematics for some  kind of device etched on the wall  hunters is decorated with the bad  batch's skull symbol while printed out  targets featuring battle droids hanged  by crosshairs bunk showing off his  prowess as a marksman  the most curious piece of decorating  however is right by the front door  as the bad batch enters the room wrecker  assumes the job of updating the team's  successful mission count  which is scratched into the wall a quick  camera pan reveals that the bad batch  has already finished 55 missions  while recker says he's adding 11 more  what does that add up to  why 66 of course which as we already  know  is a very ominous number in star wars  canon  the star wars universe isn't hurting for  unbelievably cute creatures  that goes for the cartoons too the loath  cat an adorable little predator native  to the planet lothal was introduced in  star wars rebels and has been the  animated series go-to mascot ever since  while the bad batch doesn't visit lothal  in the plot it's not too surprising that  the loft cap makes an appearance anyway  omega finds a stuffed animal while  searching the bearings and it pops up  briefly earlier in the episode  the plushie belongs to wrecker showing  us that the big brook tests a softer  side  it's also pretty clearly a loft cat  albeit one decked out in the bad batch's  signature red and black  the bad batch aren't the only divergent  clones on kamino the bad batch pilot  also introduces us to omega a young girl  who is much more than she seems  my name's amiga for one she's the first  female clone we've seen in the star wars  canon  for another she's the protege of  camino's chief medical officer  a strange position for a clone there's  clearly something special about her and  while the bad batch hasn't clued us into  what it is just yet  chances are it's something big the bad  batch is the first time we meet omega  but if you're a long time star wars fan  she might look kind of familiar  squint and omega is almost a dead ringer  for sindal tawani one of the human leads  in ewok tv movies  the wavy blonde hair the stylish  headband the ampish grin  in terms of continuity there is no  obvious link between the two characters  but it's hard to imagine the bad batch  crew didn't have cindel in mind when  designing omega  in those made for tv ewok films syndal  is the youngest daughter of a family of  settlers who crash land on the forced  moon of endor thankfully the ewoks are  always there to lend a hand  from what we've seen so far omega is  very different from sindal but there  aren't many kids who get the spotlight  in star wars so it's not a stretch to  say that they're cut from the same cloth  at least character design wise check out  one of our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about star  wars are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

